==Italian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|it|la|mēcum}} (probably through Old Italian {{m|it|conmeco}}, from Latin {{m|la|cum}} {{m|la|mēcum}}).<ref>Angelo Prati, "Vocabolario Etimologico Italiano", Torino, 1951</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{it-IPA|méco}}
* {{hyphenation|it|'''mé'''|co}}

===Preposition===
{{head|it|preposition}}

# {{lb|it|archaic|literary}} [[with]] [[me]]
#* '''1321''', [[w:Dante Alighieri|Dante Alighieri]], ''[[w:Inferno (Dante)|La divina commedia: Inferno]]'', Le Monnier (1994), Canto X, p. 155 vv. 55-56:
#*: {{quote|it|Dintorno mi guardò, come talento ¶ avesse di scoprir s'altri era '''meco'''; […]|Round me he gazed, as if solicitude ¶ he had to see if some one else were '''with me'''; […]}}
#* '''1472''', Giusto de’ Conti, ''La bella mano'', Giannalberto Tumermani (1750), p. [https://books.google.de/books?id=EqTY42Aa80kC&pg=PA122&dq=meco 122]:
#*: {{quote|it|Il cor '''meco''' s’adira, ed io con lui.|My heart gets angry '''with me''', and I with it.}}

